From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 21:09:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] sync: preserve queued actions across cancelled auth
 refresh

Reconnect refreshes authentication before rebuilding its outgoing messages.
Keep the existing queue intact across that await so cancelling the public
restart future cannot discard the evidence that an action is still unsent.
Only actions already handed to the transport fail as execution-uncertain.

Add a regression that explicitly polls and cancels auth refresh, then proves
the queued action remains eligible for its first send on the next restart.
Document that a connection-loss error does not authorize action retries.

Validation: focused formatting and whitespace checks pass. Native tests
remain unexecuted because the local resource guard rejected their disk
admission before Cargo started.
